From 3b87a519372a32372ce14674160209dc58d7c826 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: AngeloGioacchino Del Regno <angelogioacchino.delregno@somainline.org>
Date: Thu, 1 Jul 2021 12:57:22 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] cpufreq: blacklist SDM630/636/660 in cpufreq-dt-platdev

Add the SDM630, SDM636 and SDM660 to the blacklist since the CPU
scaling is handled out of this.

Signed-off-by: AngeloGioacchino Del Regno <angelogioacchino.delregno@somainline.org>
Link: https://lore.kernel.org/r/20210701105730.322718-2-angelogioacchino.delregno@somainline.org
Link: https://patchwork.kernel.org/project/linux-pm/patch/20210701105730.322718-2-angelogioacchino.delregno@somainline.org/
(cherry picked from commit 7e71d34a8bf9498ea45c715ff09ad7cc1915899b https://github.com/SoMainline/linux)
Scope: SDM630/660 common
Porting notes: Applied from the linux-pm patchwork mbox (v6 1/9, not merged upstream); the blocklist context differs on v7.3, so the three entries are placed in sorted order next to qcom,sdm670.
---
 drivers/cpufreq/cpufreq-dt-platdev.c | 3 +++
 1 file changed, 3 insertions(+)

diff --git a/drivers/cpufreq/cpufreq-dt-platdev.c b/drivers/cpufreq/cpufreq-dt-platdev.c
index 371ca1fe90..fc30800cb3 100644
--- a/drivers/cpufreq/cpufreq-dt-platdev.c
+++ b/drivers/cpufreq/cpufreq-dt-platdev.c
@@ -170,6 +170,9 @@ static const struct of_device_id blocklist[] __initconst = {
 	{ .compatible = "qcom,sc7280", },
 	{ .compatible = "qcom,sc8180x", },
 	{ .compatible = "qcom,sc8280xp", },
+	{ .compatible = "qcom,sdm630", },
+	{ .compatible = "qcom,sdm636", },
+	{ .compatible = "qcom,sdm660", },
 	{ .compatible = "qcom,sdm670", },
 	{ .compatible = "qcom,sdm845", },
 	{ .compatible = "qcom,sdx75", },
